{"timestamp": "2026-08-27T02:43:30.429+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_72ae32f4-1212-451b-85dc-0821ce6f474b", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): tell me about the fee, and how to apply for a loan, and what is the exact routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account \n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today?\n\nYou can fulfil your request using the form below.\n\nWould you still like to complete your pending Change Address request?\nUser: tell me about the fee\nAI: Sorry, I couldn't find relevant FAQ details to answer that. Could you clarify what information you are looking for?\nUser: what is the exact routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account\nAI: I don't have information available regarding: Provide the routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account..\nUser: I am asking about fees for my credit card.\nAI: I can prepare a summary for a human agent to review your request.\nUser: tell me about the fee, and how to apply for a loan, and what is the exact routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account \n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Submit the online application form along with the required income and identification documents for review.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet minimum age and income requirements to qualify for a personal loan product.\", \"conceptual\": \"A personal loan is a credit facility that provides a lump sum amount for various financial needs.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Personal_Loan\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Rewards And Promotions\"], \"customer_component\": \"Provide information on how to apply for a loan.\", \"direct_query\": \"Provide information on how to apply for a loan.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit the online application form along with the required income and identification documents for review.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet minimum age and income requirements to qualify for a personal loan product.\", \"conceptual\": \"A personal loan is a credit facility that provides a lump sum amount for various financial needs.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss loan approval timeframes, balance transfer application steps, and the ability to apply for other products after a decline, but they do not provide the requested information on how to apply for a personal loan.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_f9cce3c1\", \"fact\": \"A declined loan does not prevent applying for other Horizon Bank products.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_75ed6e4d\", \"fact\": \"Loans are typically approved and deposited into a savings account in {{faq_75ed6e4d_001}} seconds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_46c17d0e\", \"fact\": \"Balance transfer applications are initiated via the Horizon App under the Other Flexible Loans section.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_1946c44f\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps should I follow to request an Instant Loan from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App, go to the **Money** menu, and select **Loan** to initiate the process.\\n- If you are not yet a Horizon customer, first download the Horizon App, then navigate to **Product Selection** and choose **Instant Loan** to begin your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5deed8da\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for repaying my Horizon Bank loan?\\n\\nAnswer: - The loan installment is automatically posted to your Horizon credit card statement each month, and you can clear it via that statement.\\n- Open the Horizon App, navigate to Money → Credit Card, and select Pay Credit Card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0ae0bb51\", \"content\": \"Question: Do I qualify for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan offering?\\n\\nAnswer: - **For current Horizon Bank clients:**\\n  * You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_8984208c\", \"content\": \"Question: What charges does Horizon Bank apply to an Instant Loan?\\n\\nAnswer: - No annual fee is levied on Instant Loans that were originated before {{faq_8984208c_001}} February {{faq_8984208c_002}}.\\n- For Instant Loans opened on or after {{faq_8984208c_003}} February {{faq_8984208c_004}}:\\n  * A first‑year annual charge equal to {{faq_8984208c_005}} % of the loan amount is added to your Horizon credit card.\\n  * If the loan term is one year or longer, a {{faq_8984208c_006}} anniversary fee is assessed each year the loan remains outstanding, but only when the minimum payment on your Horizon credit card has not been received by its due date for the preceding {{faq_8984208c_007}} consecutive calendar months.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"procedural\": \"Locate the bank routing number on your account statement or within the secure mobile banking portal.\", \"policy\": \"Wire transfers require the correct routing number and account details to ensure successful funds processing.\", \"conceptual\": \"The routing number is a unique identifier used to direct electronic funds transfers to your account.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"Provide the routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account.\", \"direct_query\": \"Provide the routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_3\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Locate the bank routing number on your account statement or within the secure mobile banking portal.\", \"policy\": \"Wire transfers require the correct routing number and account details to ensure successful funds processing.\", \"conceptual\": \"The routing number is a unique identifier used to direct electronic funds transfers to your account.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss PayNow, payroll deposits, and local funds transfers via GIRO, but none contain information regarding the routing number for wire transfers to a deposit account.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_453239a8\", \"fact\": \"Horizon Bank savings accounts can receive payroll deposits.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_44bb339e\", \"fact\": \"Local funds transfers to Horizon Bank savings accounts can be initiated via the GIRO network.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_d8a16071\", \"content\": \"Question: Am I allowed to send or receive payments to third parties directly from my Horizon Bank Savings Pots?\\n\\nAnswer: - All external transfers—whether sending or receiving funds—must be performed using your primary Horizon Bank account. Savings Pots are not designed for direct transactions with other individuals or financial institutions.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_24638b08\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I locate my Horizon Bank account number?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App and sign in.\\n- Choose the “Savings” section.\\n- Your account number is displayed on the primary account card, following the label “Main –”.\\n- To copy it, tap the primary card and select the copy icon within the “Horizon savings account number” panel.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_fa4cba39\", \"content\": \"Question: Which personal identification number should I enter for ATM cash withdrawals, and how do I modify it?\\n\\nAnswer: - The PIN linked to your Horizon card is used for ATM withdrawals. If you have not set a PIN or wish to change it, you can do so via the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_015d7e8a\", \"content\": \"Question: What methods can I use to add funds to my Horizon savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Option {{faq_015d7e8a_001}} – Transfer via FAST**\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_002}}. Log in to your external bank’s online platform.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_003}}. Add your Horizon savings account as a local beneficiary, providing the beneficiary name and your Horizon account number.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_004}}. Initiate the FAST transfer; the amount will be credited shortly.\\n- **Option {{faq_015d7e8a_005}} – Deposit through PayNow**\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_006}}. If your mobile number or NRIC/FIN is already linked to PayNow with another bank, deregister it first.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_007}}. Open the Horizon App, go to the Payments tab, and select “Register for PayNow” if you haven’t done so.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_008}}. Complete the registration, then send a PayNow payment to your registered mobile number or NRIC/FIN, and the funds will appear in your Horizon savings account.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\" | \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"...\", \"fact\": \"...\"}]}]