u repay early, a 1% fee on the remaining outstanding amount applies.\n\n• **Cash Advances:** Withdrawing cash using your Horizon card incurs a cash advance fee of 8% on the withdrawn amount (transactions below S$5 are exempt). A daily interest rate of 0.077% (equivalent to 27.9% per annum) also applies from the posting date until full payment. From 1 July 2026, Effective Interest Rates will be tailored to individual credit profiles, ranging from 18.9% to 29.9% per annum.\n\n• **Supplementary Cards:** Horizon Bank does not levy any issuance or annual fees for an additional supplementary card.\nUser: tell me about the fee, and how to apply for a loan, and what is the exact routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account \n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Review the fee schedule by logging into the mobile app and selecting account details.\", \"policy\": \"Fees are applied based on the specific card type and the nature of the transaction.\", \"conceptual\": \"Credit card fees represent the costs associated with maintaining the account and performing specific transactions.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Fees And Charges\"], \"customer_component\": \"Provide information on credit card fees.\", \"direct_query\": \"Provide information on credit card fees.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Review the fee schedule by logging into the mobile app and selecting account details.\", \"policy\": \"Fees are applied based on the specific card type and the nature of the transaction.\", \"conceptual\": \"Credit card fees represent the costs associated with maintaining the account and performing specific transactions.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_5f31fc26\", \"content\": \"Question: What factors determine the monthly fee for transferring my balance to a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, the monthly charge for balance transfers is calculated based on the outstanding balance. Prior to the final month of your tenure, a monthly fee of either {{faq_5f31fc26_001}} for transfers approved before August {{faq_5f31fc26_002}}, {{faq_5f31fc26_003}}, or {{faq_5f31fc26_004}} for transfers approved on or after August {{faq_5f31fc26_005}}, {{faq_5f31fc26_006}}, will be applied to your Horizon Bank credit card statement. This fee will be included in the minimum payment due. In the last month of your tenure, or if you opt to repay your balance early, the remaining outstanding balance will be charged to your statement, along with a {{faq_5f31fc26_007}} fee on the outstanding amount, which will also be included in the minimum payment due. For detailed information, please consult the Balance Transfer Product Terms and Key Facts document provided by Horizon Bank.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_e5db6d91\", \"content\": \"Question: Are there any fees associated with obtaining a supplementary Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank does not levy any issuance or annual fees for an additional card. All expenses incurred on the supplementary card are combined with the primary card’s balance, and any late‑payment penalties or interest charges are applied exclusively to the main cardholder.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_25ce7c68\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for requesting a waiver of charges on my Horizon Bank credit card account?\\n\\nAnswer: To request a waiver of a late payment fee, simply send a message through the Horizon App's in-app chat service, specifying 'fee waiver' in your query. Our team will carefully review your request and provide an update via push notification within {{faq_25ce7c68_001}} working days.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_df0e6cbd\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the charges associated with withdrawing cash using my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: As of {{faq_df0e6cbd_001}} February {{faq_df0e6cbd_002}}, Horizon Bank imposes a cash advance fee of {{faq_df0e6cbd_003}} on the withdrawn amount, although transactions below {{faq_df0e6cbd_004}} are exempt from this charge. Additionally, a daily interest rate of {{faq_df0e6cbd_005}} (equivalent to {{faq_df0e6cbd_006}} per annum) is applied to the withdrawn amount, starting from the transaction posting date until the payment is made in full. Please note that from {{faq_df0e6cbd_007}} July {{faq_df0e6cbd_008}}, your Effective Interest Rate will be tailored to your individual credit profile, ranging from {{faq_df0e6cbd_009}} to {{faq_df0e6cbd_010}} per annum.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Submit the required identification and income documents through the online portal to begin the review.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet the minimum age and income requirements to qualify for a personal loan.\", \"conceptual\": \"A personal loan is a credit facility that provides a lump sum of cash for various needs.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Personal_Loan\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\"], \"customer_component\": \"Explain the application process for a loan.\", \"direct_query\": \"Explain the application process for a loan.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit the required identification and income documents through the online portal to begin the review.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet the minimum age and income requirements to qualify for a personal loan.\", \"conceptual\": \"A personal loan is a credit facility that provides a lump sum of cash for various needs.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_75ed6e4d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical timeframe for my loan to be approved?\\n\\nAnswer: - The vast majority of loans are approved and the amount is deposited into your Horizon savings account in about {{faq_75ed6e4d_001}} seconds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_f9cce3c1\", \"content\": \"Question: If my Instant Loan request is declined, can I still submit applications for other Horizon Bank products such as a credit card or a savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - Absolutely. A declined loan does not prevent you from applying for other Horizon Bank offerings. You simply need to start a new application tailored to the specific product you wish to obtain.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_46c17d0e\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps do I need to take to initiate a balance transfer request with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To begin the balance transfer process, navigate to the Horizon App, select the 'More' option, and then proceed to the 'Loan' section, where you will find 'Other Flexible Loans' to commence your application.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"procedural\": \"Locate the bank identification code and account number within your digital banking dashboard for incoming transfers.\", \"policy\": \"Wire transfers require the correct bank routing number to ensure funds are credited to the account.\", \"conceptual\": \"A routing number is a unique identifier used to direct electronic funds to the correct financial institution.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Payments And Transfers\"], \"customer_component\": \"Provide the routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account.\", \"direct_query\": \"Provide the routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_3\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Locate the bank identification code and account number within your digital banking dashboard for incoming transfers.\", \"policy\": \"Wire transfers require the correct bank routing number to ensure funds are credited to the account.\", \"conceptual\": \"A routing number is a unique identifier used to direct electronic funds to the correct financial institution.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_c0c586c8\", \"content\": \"Question: I’ve already linked my mobile number (or NRIC) to another bank for PayNow receipts. Can I also associate that same mobile number with my Horizon Bank account for PayNow?\\n\\nAnswer: - Yes, you may. However, you must first remove the existing association of your mobile number (or NRIC) with the other bank’s account before linking it to your Horizon Bank account.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_453239a8\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to designate my Horizon Bank savings account as the recipient account for my payroll deposits?\\n\\nAnswer: Indeed, you can notify your employer to deposit your salary into your Horizon Bank savings account. Horizon Bank is now equipped to handle incoming salary payments, ensuring a seamless and efficient process.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_44bb339e\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I transfer funds from another bank to my Horizon Bank savings account if I don't want to use the FAST service?\\n\\nAnswer: You have the option to initiate a local funds transfer through the GIRO network from other banks to your specified Horizon Bank savings account. Please note that transfers using MEPS+ or RTGS are not available for this type of transaction.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_05669a00\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I arrange for recurring transfers to other bank accounts through Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, you can effortlessly set up recurring transfers to other bank accounts using our convenient AutoPay feature. To do so, follow these simple steps: \\n   - Access your Horizon App and navigate to the 'Payments' section, then choose either 'Bank Transfer' or 'Credit Card' to pay other banks' savings accounts or credit cards. \\n   - Add or select your payee, enter the transfer amount, and specify the desired schedule and frequency. \\n   - Confirm your details and complete the setup. \\n   Alternatively, you can also utilize the PayNow feature within the Horizon App by selecting 'PayNow' from the homepage, adding your payee, and configuring the transfer details. \\n   For a more streamlined experience, access the 'AutoPay' option under 'Payments', choose your saved payee, and input the necessary transfer information, including the amount, purpose, and transfer frequency.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or