zon Bank Savings Pots?\\n\\nAnswer: - All external transfers—whether sending or receiving funds—must be performed using your primary Horizon Bank account. Savings Pots are not designed for direct transactions with other individuals or financial institutions.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_24638b08\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I locate my Horizon Bank account number?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App and sign in.\\n- Choose the “Savings” section.\\n- Your account number is displayed on the primary account card, following the label “Main –”.\\n- To copy it, tap the primary card and select the copy icon within the “Horizon savings account number” panel.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_fa4cba39\", \"content\": \"Question: Which personal identification number should I enter for ATM cash withdrawals, and how do I modify it?\\n\\nAnswer: - The PIN linked to your Horizon card is used for ATM withdrawals. If you have not set a PIN or wish to change it, you can do so via the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_015d7e8a\", \"content\": \"Question: What methods can I use to add funds to my Horizon savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Option {{faq_015d7e8a_001}} – Transfer via FAST**\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_002}}. Log in to your external bank’s online platform.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_003}}. Add your Horizon savings account as a local beneficiary, providing the beneficiary name and your Horizon account number.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_004}}. Initiate the FAST transfer; the amount will be credited shortly.\\n- **Option {{faq_015d7e8a_005}} – Deposit through PayNow**\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_006}}. If your mobile number or NRIC/FIN is already linked to PayNow with another bank, deregister it first.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_007}}. Open the Horizon App, go to the Payments tab, and select “Register for PayNow” if you haven’t done so.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_008}}. Complete the registration, then send a PayNow payment to your registered mobile number or NRIC/FIN, and the funds will appear in your Horizon savings accoun