ansaction.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_fa4cba39\", \"content\": \"Question: Which personal identification number should I enter for ATM cash withdrawals, and how do I modify it?\\n\\nAnswer: - The PIN linked to your Horizon card is used for ATM withdrawals. If you have not set a PIN or wish to change it, you can do so via the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_015d7e8a\", \"content\": \"Question: What methods can I use to add funds to my Horizon savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Option {{faq_015d7e8a_001}} – Transfer via FAST**\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_002}}. Log in to your external bank’s online platform.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_003}}. Add your Horizon savings account as a local beneficiary, providing the beneficiary name and your Horizon account number.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_004}}. Initiate the FAST transfer; the amount will be credited shortly.\\n- **Option {{faq_015d7e8a_005}} – Deposit through PayNow**\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_006}}. If your mobile number or NRIC/FIN is already linked to PayNow with another bank, deregister it first.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_007}}. Open the Horizon App, go to the Payments tab, and select “Register for PayNow” if you haven’t done so.\\n  {{faq_015d7e8a_008}}. Complete the registration, then send a PayNow payment to your registered mobile number or NRIC/FIN, and the funds will appear in your Horizon savings account.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_05669a00\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I arrange for recurring transfers to other bank accounts through Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, you can effortlessly set up recurring transfers to other bank accounts using our convenient AutoPay feature. To do so, follow these simple steps: \\n   - Access your Horizon App and navigate to the 'Payments' section, then choose either 'Bank Transfer' or 'Credit Card' to pay other banks' savings accounts or credit cards. \\n   - Add or select your payee, enter the transfer amount, and specify the desired schedule and frequency. \\n   - Confirm your details and complete the setup. \\n   Alternatively, you can also utilize the PayNow feature within the Horizon App by selecting 'PayNow' from the homepage, adding your payee, and configuring the transfer details. \\n   For a more streamlined experience, access the 'AutoPay' option under 'Payments', choose your saved payee, and input the necessary transfer information, including the amount, purpose, and transfer frequency.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can