{"timestamp": "2026-08-27T04:23:05.455+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_a003c00f-8518-4501-80b3-d7d918feb1c4", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): tell me about the fee, and how to apply for a loan, and what is the exact routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account \n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today?\n\nYou can fulfil your request using the form below.\nUser: tell me about the fee, and how to apply for a loan, and what is the exact routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account \n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Locate your routing number on your monthly account statement or within the account details section online.\", \"policy\": \"Routing numbers are specific to the bank and are required for all incoming and outgoing wire transfers.\", \"conceptual\": \"A routing number is a unique nine-digit code used to identify a financial institution during electronic transactions.\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"Deposit_Account\", \"Horizon_APP\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"Provide the routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account.\", \"direct_query\": \"Provide the routing number for wire transfers to my deposit account.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_3\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Locate your routing number on your monthly account statement or within the account details section online.\", \"policy\": \"Routing numbers are specific to the bank and are required for all incoming and outgoing wire transfers.\", \"conceptual\": \"A routing number is a unique nine-digit code used to identify a financial institution during electronic transactions.\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Access your digital banking dashboard to view specific electronic transfer instructions for your active deposit account.\", \"policy\": \"Verify that the receiving institution accepts standard electronic wire transfers before initiating any funds movement request.\", \"conceptual\": \"The routing transit number serves as the primary identifier for processing domestic electronic fund transfers between banks.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss credit card payment procedures, bank identification codes (BIC/Bank Code), and recurring deposits, but none provide the routing number for wire transfers to a deposit account.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"None of the provided parents contain information regarding the routing number for wire transfers; they only discuss account numbers, PayNow, and savings pots.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss methods for transferring funds into a savings account (FAST, PayNow, GIRO) and ATM PIN management, but none contain information regarding the routing number for wire transfers to a deposit account.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_02489175\", \"content\": \"Question: What information will be displayed when I initiate a payment to a recipient through Horizon Bank's digital banking services?\\n\\nAnswer: When sending funds to an individual recipient, you will notice that only a portion of their name is visible after entering their PayNow proxy. However, for corporate recipients, the full registered company name will be displayed as usual. This applies to all PayNow transactions, including those made using the Scan to Pay feature within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_95665e33\", \"content\": \"Question: How do I locate my Horizon Bank account number within the app?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App and sign in.\\n- Navigate to the **Savings** tab.\\n- Your account number appears on the primary account card under the \\\"Main\\\" heading.\\n- To copy it, tap the card and select the copy icon shown in the \\\"Horizon savings account number\\\" panel.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_ad98a5ba\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the details of Horizon Bank's Signature deposit plan?\\n\\nAnswer: - The Horizon Signature account provides a maximum annual interest of {{faq_ad98a5ba_001}} on the first {{faq_ad98a5ba_002}} million of your balance, composed of:\\n  • A base rate of {{faq_ad98a5ba_003}} per year, applied without any conditions;\\n  • A spend‑bonus of {{faq_ad98a5ba_004}} per year for Horizon Union members (or {{faq_ad98a5ba_005}} for non‑members) when you complete five qualifying {{faq_ad98a5ba_006}} card transactions in a month;\\n  • A balance‑bonus of {{faq_ad98a5ba_007}} per year once the account maintains an average daily balance of at least {{faq_ad98a5ba_008}} during the month;\\n  • A salary‑bonus of {{faq_ad98a5ba_009}} per year if a single GIRO credit of a minimum of {{faq_ad98a5ba_010}} is posted in the month.\\n- Any portion of the balance that exceeds {{faq_ad98a5ba_011}} million earns only the base rate of {{faq_ad98a5ba_012}} per year.\\n- Interest is credited to the account on the last day of each month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6e200634\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the details of Horizon Bank's Signature deposit plan?\\n\\nAnswer: - The Signature plan lets you earn up to {{faq_6e200634_001}} per annum on the first {{faq_6e200634_002}} million of your deposit balance. The rate is built from several components:\\n  * A base interest of {{faq_6e200634_003}} p.a. that applies automatically;\\n  * A spend‑bonus of {{faq_6e200634_004}} p.a. for NTUC Union members (or {{faq_6e200634_005}} p.a. for non‑members) when you complete five qualifying {{faq_6e200634_006}} card transactions within the month;\\n  * A balance‑bonus of {{faq_6e200634_007}} p.a. once your average daily balance for the month reaches {{faq_6e200634_008}};\\n  * A salary‑bonus of {{faq_6e200634_009}} p.a. if you receive a minimum salary credit of {{faq_6e200634_010}} in a single GIRO transaction during the month.\\n- Any portion of the balance that exceeds {{faq_6e200634_011}} million earns interest at the base rate of {{faq_6e200634_012}} p.a.\\n- Interest is credited on the last day of each month.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\" | \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"...\", \"fact\": \"...\"}]}]}\n        "}
