ent\": \"Question: What documentation is required to initiate a Horizon Bank credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: To streamline your credit card application with Horizon Bank, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can utilize MyInfo for expedited form completion. For foreign applicants, please ensure you have your passport and most recent payslip readily available for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_adff3913\", \"content\": \"Question: After I complete my credit card application through a partner or affiliate platform, what steps follow?\\n\\nAnswer: - You will receive an immediate notification of the decision via email or SMS.\\n- If the application is approved, the message will contain instructions for logging into the Horizon App and activating your new Horizon card.\\n- If the application is declined, you will be informed of the outcome through an email or text.\\n- When a decision cannot be made instantly or additional documentation is required, we will email you with directions to access the Horizon App, review your pending status, and upload the needed documents.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_dea282b8\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for using Horizon Bank’s online credit‑card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Initiate a Horizon credit‑card request through a partner’s mobile app or website.\\n- The submission is handled on a secure Horizon Bank web portal.\\n- Utilize the MyInfo service to auto‑populate your personal details.\\n- Receive immediate status updates, and be prompted for any additional actions required within the Horizon App.\"}]}]\n    Intent clarification inputs -- each already carries the underlying\n    question to convey (in your own words, per the rule below) in its own\n    \"clarification_evidence\" field, and any tappable reply guesses in\n    \"candidate_replies\": []\n    No-info inputs -- each is a search that was genuinely attempted but\n    found nothing; each already carries the underlying statement to convey\n    (in your own words, per the rule below) in its own \"no_info_evidence\"\n    field: []\n    Terminal unresolved task markers (topic/status only; never evidence): []\n    Decline inputs -- each already carries the underlying sentence to\n    convey (in your own words, per the rule below) in its own\n    \"decline_evidence\" field: []\n    Available shortcuts this turn (each is either a \"form\" -- a guided\n    service request the customer could complete instead of the manual FAQ\n    steps -- or \"navigation\" -- a direct in-app link to the relevant screen.\n    Each button is attached automatically and unconditionally; you do not\n    control whether it appears, only whether your text acknowledges it):\n    [{\"kind\": \"form\", \"label\": \"Resubmit KYC Document\", \"topic\": \"Resubmit an identity document for an existing customer's KYC record.\", \"for_request\": \"How to update KYC (Know Your Customer) documentation\"}]\n    Unavailable service requests (could not be registered this turn; state\n    only the supplied reason, never guess why): []\n    Verified customer-specific facts (each is a pre-verified fact about this\n    specific customer, safe to state directly and confidently, on the same\n    footing as approved evidence): []\n    Personal data references (each is a specific personal-data value already\n    fetched and authorized for this customer this turn; you never see the\n    real value, only an opaque insert_token):\n    []\n    Failed outbound-audit feedback (constraints only, never evidence). Each\n    entry identifies one specific claim or instruction to remove — it is\n    never permission to abandon the topic it came from. After removing\n    exactly what is flagged, re-apply every Design Principle below to still\n    give the most complete, honestly-scoped response the remaining approved\n    evidence supports:\n    [\"Grounding violations (internal constraints only; never