rience Centre for in‑person identity verification. Bring the original identification documents:\\n  • NRIC for Singapore citizens or permanent residents.\\n  • Passport for Work Pass or Dependent Pass holders.\\n- A Horizon representative will confirm your identity and continue processing your request.\\n- You can monitor the application’s progress through the Horizon App.\\n- From {{faq_5b37494f_003}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_004}} onward, we advise using MyInfo authentication for a faster, more secure submission. Ensure your SingPass details are up‑to‑date before applying.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_76c34cea\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it required to book an appointment before visiting the Horizon Experience Centre for in‑person identity verification?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you submitted a manual application before {{faq_76c34cea_001}} December {{faq_76c34cea_002}}, you may attend without scheduling an appointment.\\n- From {{faq_76c34cea_003}} December {{faq_76c34cea_004}} onward, we recommend completing the application via MyInfo authentication, which is faster and more secure. Ensure your SingPass details are current before you apply.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_73ee8e91\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to open a Horizon Bank account without using MyInfo authentication?\\n\\nAnswer: - Effective {{faq_73ee8e91_001}} December {{faq_73ee8e91_002}}, all new Horizon Bank accounts must be created using MyInfo verification. This requirement speeds up onboarding and eliminates the need for paper‑based applications. Should you remove or reinstall the Horizon App after completing registration, you will be required to log in again via Singpass for authentication.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_dea282b8\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for using Horizon Bank’s online credit‑card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Initiate a Horizon credit‑card request through a partner’s mobile app or website.\\n- The submission is handled on a secure Horizon Bank web portal.\\n- Utilize the MyInfo service to auto‑populate your personal details.\\n- Receive immediate status updates, and be prompted for any additional actions required within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_10f9fec0\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements to open a new Horizon Bank account?\\n\\nAnswer: To initiate the application process for a Horizon Bank account, simply utilize your mobile device and authenticate through MyInfo, which will expedite the pre-filling of your application in a secure manner. For non-Singaporean residents, please be prepared to upload a valid passport and relevant income documentation, particularly if you are applying for a Horizon credit card.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT mer