\nAnswer: - Updating your personal information can now be done directly through the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_24568045_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_24568045_002}}. Tap the Profile icon located at the upper‑right corner.\\n{{faq_24568045_003}}. Within Profile, navigate to Settings ► Personal Details.\\n{{faq_24568045_004}}. Choose the field you wish to modify (address, phone number, or email).\\n{{faq_24568045_005}}. For phone number or email changes, enter the one‑time password (OTP) sent to you.\\n{{faq_24568045_006}}. Provide your Horizon Key for additional verification before the update is applied.\\n{{faq_24568045_007}}. After you submit, the change will be processed within {{faq_24568045_008}} hours for phone numbers and email addresses, while address updates take effect instantly.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d6102e00\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to customize the masking of my name in the Horizon Bank's PayNow service?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we have implemented a standardized approach to PayNow naming conventions, taking into account both industry standards and customer feedback. As a result, the updated PayNow name is applied uniformly across the board, and individual modifications are not permitted to ensure consistency.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0765b6e6\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for pairing my Horizon card with an account?\\n\\nAnswer: - Card pairing is a capability that allows you to link your Horizon Link card to either your Horizon Link credit‑card account or your Horizon savings account, provided you hold both products.\\n- To change the association:\\n  * From credit‑card account to savings account: Open the Horizon App, navigate to \\\"View and manage card,\\\" tap the \\\"Pair card\\\" button, and select \\\"Pair with savings account.\\\" After this change, all purchases—including any pre‑existing automatic payments—will be drawn from your savings account.\\n  * From savings account to credit‑card account: In the same \\\"View and manage card\\\" section, tap \\\"Pair card\\\" and choose \\\"Pair with credit card account.\\\" Subsequent transactions, including recurring payments, will be charged to your credit‑card account and will appear on your next statement.\\n- ATM cash withdrawals: When using the card at an ATM you may elect to withdraw funds from either your savings account or your credit‑card account. To avoid cash‑advance fees, we recommend keeping the card paired with your savings account and selecting \\\"Savings Account\\\" for ATM withdrawals, even if the machine does not explicitly offer a savings option. If you opt to withdraw using the credit‑card side, a cash‑advance fee (effective {{faq_0765b6e6_001}} Feb {{faq_0765b6e6_002}}) and associated interest will be applied.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_65f94a35\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to reallocate a recent purchase made with my Horizon Bank debit card to my Horizon Bank credit card account instead?\\n\\nAnswer: Once a transaction has been approved and is in the process of being settled, it cannot be altered. Consequently, the charge will remain on your Horizon Bank debit card account.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents 