its held by non‑bank depositors are protected by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation up to {{faq_1b9ab045_012}} per depositor across all Scheme members, as mandated by law.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_dea282b8\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for using Horizon Bank’s online credit‑card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Initiate a Horizon credit‑card request through a partner’s mobile app or website.\\n- The submission is handled on a secure Horizon Bank web portal.\\n- Utilize the MyInfo service to auto‑populate your personal details.\\n- Receive immediate status updates, and be prompted for any additional actions required within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_85dbaadf\", \"content\": \"Question: What documentation is required to initiate a Horizon Bank credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: To streamline your credit card application with Horizon Bank, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can utilize MyInfo for expedited form completion. For foreign applicants, please ensure you have your passport and most recent payslip readily available for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b3c9ded6\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements for applying for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be considered for a Horizon Bank credit card, you must meet specific criteria. If you are a Singaporean citizen or permanent resident between the ages of {{faq_b3c9ded6_001}} and {{faq_b3c9ded6_002}}, you will need to have an annual income of at least {{faq_b3c9ded6_003}}. For foreigners with a valid work pass, the requirement is an annual income of {{faq_b3c9ded6_004}}. Alternatively, if you are above {{faq_b3c9ded6_005}} years old, the annual income requirements are {{faq_b3c9ded6_006}} for Singaporean citizens or permanent residents, and {{faq_b3c9ded6_007}} for foreigners with a valid work pass.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.cust