{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T05:40:03.815+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_2c022427-3876-4f70-9bc8-6ac0bd8ab7b8", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): so what will happen if my credit card application got rejected?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: I am asking about re-applying for a credit card.\nAI: I do not currently have the details available regarding the process for re-applying for a credit card. 💳\nUser: i just want to know can i apply again if got rejected\nAI: I currently do not have any details available about whether you can apply again for a credit card following an earlier denial. 💳\nUser: so what will happen if my credit card application got rejected?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Steps to follow after receiving a notification of credit card application rejection from the bank.\", \"policy\": \"Rules regarding waiting periods and eligibility criteria for re-submitting a new credit card application.\", \"conceptual\": \"General information about the credit card application review process and reasons for potential application denial.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\"], \"customer_component\": \"Explain the consequences or process following a credit card application rejection.\", \"direct_query\": \"Explain the consequences or process following a credit card application rejection.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Steps to follow after receiving a notification of credit card application rejection from the bank.\", \"policy\": \"Rules regarding waiting periods and eligibility criteria for re-submitting a new credit card application.\", \"conceptual\": \"General information about the credit card application review process and reasons for potential application denial.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"content\": \"Question: Why did Horizon Bank reject my credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Every credit card request undergoes an internal review, and we evaluate each submission thoroughly. Typical reasons for a denial include:\\n- Insufficient earnings:\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_001}}‑{{faq_1b9ab045_002}} with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_003}}\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_004}}+ with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_005}}\\n  • Non‑resident ({{faq_1b9ab045_006}} years or older) earning less than {{faq_1b9ab045_007}} annually\\n- Having already reached the maximum credit exposure allowed across all banks\\n- Existing overdue obligations with other financial institutions\\n- Absence of a recent Notice of Assessment or CPF contribution record\\n- Applicant is younger than {{faq_1b9ab045_008}} years old\\n\\nIf you were declined, you may still consider opening a Horizon savings account, which offers up to {{faq_1b9ab045_009}} p.a. on the first {{faq_1b9ab045_010}} deposited and can provide up to an {{faq_1b9ab045_011}} return when paired with a Horizon debit card (subject to terms and conditions). To start the savings account application, simply:\\n- Uninstall the Horizon App\\n- Re‑install the Horizon App from the app store\\n- Submit a savings‑account request through the app\\n\\nPlease note that Singapore‑dollar deposits held by non‑bank depositors are protected by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation up to {{faq_1b9ab045_012}} per depositor across all Scheme members, as mandated by law.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_742db265\", \"content\": \"Question: How does my existing credit limit with another bank impact my Horizon Bank credit card application as a regulated customer?\\n\\nAnswer: When applying for a Horizon Bank credit card, your overall credit limit is considered across all unsecured credit facilities, including those with other banks. For instance, if your monthly income is {{faq_742db265_001}}, your total credit limit would be {{faq_742db265_002}}, which is four times your monthly income. If you have an existing credit limit of {{faq_742db265_003}} with another bank, Horizon Bank can offer you a credit limit of up to {{faq_742db265_004}}. To determine your credit limit, you can either allow Horizon Bank to decide or choose your own credit limit. To explore these options in more detail, consider the following steps:\\n   * To have Horizon Bank determine your credit limit, review the assigned limit and adjust as needed.\\n   * To select your own credit limit, which may be higher than the assigned limit, follow the prompts to input your preferred amount.\\n   * If you are satisfied with the assigned credit limit, simply confirm and proceed with your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_adff3913\", \"content\": \"Question: After I complete my credit card application through a partner or affiliate platform, what steps follow?\\n\\nAnswer: - You will receive an immediate notification of the decision via email or SMS.\\n- If the application is approved, the message will contain instructions for logging into the Horizon App and activating your new Horizon card.\\n- If the application is declined, you will be informed of the outcome through an email or text.\\n- When a decision cannot be made instantly or additional documentation is required, we will email you with directions to access the Horizon App, review your pending status, and upload the needed documents.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_dea282b8\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for using Horizon Bank’s online credit‑card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Initiate a Horizon credit‑card request through a partner’s mobile app or website.\\n- The submission is handled on a secure Horizon Bank web portal.\\n- Utilize the MyInfo service to auto‑populate your personal details.\\n- Receive immediate status updates, and be prompted for any additional actions required within the Horizon App.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n         