ed limit, your credit limit will be adjusted accordingly. Should your outstanding balance surpass the revised credit limit, you will be required to settle the excess amount to avoid applicable charges.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_adff3913\", \"content\": \"Question: After I complete my credit card application through a partner or affiliate platform, what steps follow?\\n\\nAnswer: - You will receive an immediate notification of the decision via email or SMS.\\n- If the application is approved, the message will contain instructions for logging into the Horizon App and activating your new Horizon card.\\n- If the application is declined, you will be informed of the outcome through an email or text.\\n- When a decision cannot be made instantly or additional documentation is required, we will email you with directions to access the Horizon App, review your pending status, and upload the needed documents.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First id